tools.description:
Use this tool when you need to ask the user questions during execution. This allows you to: 1. Gather user preferences or requirements, 2. Clarify ambiguous instructions, 3. Get decisions on implementation choices, 4. Offer choices to the user about what direction to take. An 'Other' option that allows free-form input is automatically provided to the user, so do NOT include 'Other' or similar options in your options array. If you want to ask a question referring to work you did (e.g., a plan you wrote), you must write that work as a message to the user AND end your turn (give them a chance to read and respond) BEFORE using this tool.

Example:
{ "questions": [
  { "question": "Should the frobnosticator run on startup?", "options": ["Yes, run automatically", "No, only on demand"] },
  { "question": "Where should the thingamajig be displayed?", "options": ["In the sidebar", "In the top bar", "In a popover"] }
] }

